# Submodule reference for ToneFill ARA.
#
# This file is intentionally left as a COMMENTED reference so it does not collide with the
# `git submodule add` commands in docs/SETUP.md (which write their own entries). After you run
# the setup steps, your real .gitmodules will contain the two active blocks shown below.
#
# Mandatory submodules: JUCE + ARA_SDK only.
#   * VST3 SDK is NOT a submodule — JUCE ships VST3 support in its own tree.
#   * Catch2 is fetched by tests/CMakeLists.txt via FetchContent (no submodule).
#
# Pins (see docs/SETUP.md for the exact commands and how to verify compatibility):
#
# [submodule "external/JUCE"]
#     path = external/JUCE
#     url  = https://github.com/juce-framework/JUCE.git
#     # pinned commit: tag 7.0.12 (last JUCE 7.0.x; has IS_ARA_EFFECT + juce_set_ara_sdk_path)
#
# [submodule "external/ARA_SDK"]
#     path = external/ARA_SDK
#     url  = https://github.com/Celemony/ARA_SDK.git
#     # pinned commit: an ARA 2.x release tag compatible with the JUCE pin above
#     #                (list with `git -C external/ARA_SDK tag`; see SETUP.md)
